= The German order book contracts

The export slowdown has already reached Silesian factories, logistics firms
and component suppliers through a mandatory dated event. Berlin is both a
negotiating partner and a convenient villain. This one-shot card decides
whether the Left owns industrial security or merely comments on Germany; it
does not apply the slowdown again.

- @workers
- @investment
- @blame

@workers
title: Demand wage insurance, shorter hours and union seats in restructuring
subtitle: Labour credibility +5 and household security +3; fiscal stress +3.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 5; workers_support += 4; household_security += 3; fiscal_stress += 3; budget_promises += 1; germany_relation += 2; news_headline = "Workers receive an industrial shield before shareholders receive an exit"

The plan is expensive and immediately useful. Employers complain that the
Left has turned a trade cycle into a collective-bargaining campaign.

- #poland_card_finish

@investment
title: Build an EU industrial-investment and procurement coalition
subtitle: Germany +5, EU influence +4 and growth +0.4; coalition liberals gain leverage.
on-arrival: germany_relation += 5; eu_influence += 4; eu_institutional_trust += 2; economic_growth += 0.4; government_delivery += 2 if left_in_government = 1; ko_relation += 2; labor_dissent += 2; news_headline = "The slowdown produces a European industrial investment table"

Joint procurement, grids, rail and clean-industry finance preserve orders.
Unions support the work and ask who will own the assets and set the wage floor.

- #poland_card_finish

@blame
title: Make Berlin answer for Poland's lost shifts
subtitle: Immediate salience; Germany −8, far-right agenda +4 and EU influence −3.
on-arrival: germany_relation -= 8; eu_influence -= 3; pis_relation += 2; rural_support += 1; public_trust += 1; far_right_agenda += 4; konf_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "An anti-German campaign outruns the industrial plan"

The attack travels faster than the policy and validates the parties that have
spent years treating every European dispute as a national humiliation.

- #poland_card_finish
